			<div class="content" id="post-content-1754291">
									

<p>&quot;Lip reading&quot; is not actually something people can do. A large part of speech is tongue and throat movements that are not visible from the outside. At best you pick up about 20% of what was said. If you want to communicate effectively there has to be some sort of writing involved. It would be easy talking to it, but getting its responses back would require a decoding process.</p>

