<p>Talking to it would be as simple as using a whiteboard, perhaps with a note that scientific concepts can be in English while conversation speech should be in Portugese. It talking to you would involve writing the best guess from lip reading on the white board and getting confirmation (eye blinks?) on every word. If you wanted to get more technical you could include a code book where longer words or scientific concepts were communicated using simpler words. Like &quot;code 1&#160;5&quot;; &quot;code&quot; being the delineator, &quot;1&quot; meaning planet and the following &quot;5&quot; meaning Jupiter. Details would probably clog up the article so mentioning the white board and the code book should be enough.</p>

